From bf19272c42be75114e68669371f3ecb97427a15c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Destrudos6 <3411622425@qq.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 13:52:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add tap-to-lookup words in the bilingual reader

Reading a transcript is the moment unknown words actually appear,
so every word of the original line is now tappable: tapping it
opens a dictionary popup filled by the Youdao web dictionary API
(dict.youdao.com/jsonapi, the same endpoint the Youdao web client
uses; field mapping cross-checked against the easydict open-source
implementation). The popup shows the phonetic transcription - which
plays the pronunciation clip when tapped - the exam labels, the
per-sense translations, the word forms and web translations as a
fallback for phrases, plus a button that saves the word into a
local word book (stored in the default shared preferences, so it
rides along in every export and cloud backup and is ready for a
later export to a spaced-repetition app).

Lookup results are kept in an LRU cache, so re-tapping a word
while reading is instant and free. Word boundaries keep embedded
apostrophes and hyphens (don't, good-looking); single letters are
skipped except a/I. The translation line stays plain: tapping is
for the learning side of the pair, not the meaning the learner
already has.
